WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Good morning John; it's Monday.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:06.609
I have to say, yesterday: fantastic day. I
just had a great day yesterday. It was the

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:11.210
first of May, and true to Jonathan Coulton's
song, it was a gorgeous day outside, though

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:16.660
I did not have any al fresco fornication,
nor did I witness any, thank goodness. Katherine

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.269
and I went and got breakfast downtown, we
ran into some friends who were filming a movie,

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:24.710
and I got to be in their movie. We went to
see Win Win, the new Paul Giamatti m- awesome,

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.830
really good movie. I read Clash of Kings on
my back porch, Osama bin Laden was killed

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.890
in a precision military strike, Katherine
and I played Mario Kart Wii...

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.560
Actually, we were playing Mario Kart Wii;
Katherine had to go to the bathroom, I pull

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.750
out my phone to check Twitter, and by the
time she got back I had my laptop on my lap,

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.120
and I was watching Obama's address, with the
Mario Kart music in the background.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.400
Obama: [with Mario Kart menu music] The United
States has conducted an operation that killed

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.820
Osama bin Laden, the leader of al-Qaeda.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.940
Hank: It was a surreal moment. And, I'm not
gonna lie, Katherine and I high-fived. And

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.970
then we, uh, raced in the 100cc Banana Cup;
I was Donkey Kong, she was Yoshi, and... she

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:57.970
won.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.210
So there are all kinds of interesting discussions
that I'm sure people will be having over the

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:05.080
coming days. Like, for example, is it okay
to high-five your wife over the death of another

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.600
human being? But instead of that discussion,
since, y'know, this happened, like, mere hours

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.030
ago - it seems a little premature to talk
about all the implications - let's just talk

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:18.030
for a moment about what we actually know before
we launch into the, uh, spin cycle.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.810
Number one, despite the fact that Jack Bauer
was a trending topic on Twitter last night,

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.640
the death of Osama bin Laden had nothing to
do with rogue agents or weird intelligence

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:30.600
activities or breaking international treaties
or torture, which is a really notoriously

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.750
bad information gathering technique. And there
weren't even any twenty-four hour deadlines;

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:39.210
it was a long, thought-out, months-long process.
They gathered information over a long period

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.310
of time, and they put all that information
together using some great deductive minds,

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.610
and they, they figured it out.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:49.950
Number two, CIA operatives and the Navy SEALs
involved in the action attempted to take Osama

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.190
bin Laden alive but were not able to. It is
unclear, uh, when this will be made in to

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.880
a made-for-TV movie, but my guess is minimum
six months. Five people were killed in the

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.200
attack, four of them were al-Qaeda members,
one of them was a woman who was used as a

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.460
human shield by one of those al-Qaeda members,
which is horrible.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.880
Ayman al-Zawahri remains the number-one guy
at al-Qaeda, and he's been sort of the chief

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.470
of operations guy for a long time, and he's
a jerk, but according to what I've read and

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:19.400
various leaked documents from the CIA, he
doesn't have the same charismatic following.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:24.230
It might be hard for him to keep the loyalty
that- that Osama bin Laden was kind of holding

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:27.440
together at al-Qaeda, so this could be a pretty
good thing.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.240
And lastly, Barack Obama ordered this assault
right before flying to Alabama to survey the

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.550
damage done by the tornadoes and talk to the
people there, and then during the attack itself

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.320
he called the president of Pakistan. He was
like "Hey, president of Pakistan, just wanted

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.490
you to know we found bin Laden; we're coming
to get him; we're either gonna take him captive

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:46.660
or we're gonna kill him. And, uh, sorry for
not asking permission, but yeah, we're just

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:51.959
gonna do this." And that is a phone call that
I cannot imagine Donald Trump making, so...

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:55.330
glad Barack Obama was in charge just then.
That's just me, though.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:59.910
I apologize for not, y'know, waxing poetic
as John probably would have about the, you

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:05.270
know, emotions of our country, about the morality
of assassination, as we receive this, ah,

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:09.739
cold-served dish. As for how I feel personally,
my emotions are in a lot of different places

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:13.709
right now. So let's just say this, uh, the
fact that I know that I should not be happy

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:18.480
at the death of another human being, uh, that
doesn't change the fact that I am.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.760
John, I'll see you on Wednesday.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.650
End screen! Sorry, not a very light-hearted
video, that. But, y'know. I have to say one

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:29.860
thing here, in John's last video, uh, lots
of people asked a question and then got 125

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.630
or so thumbs up, that question did, and that
question was "When is Hank's first album coming

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:40.790
out?!" and... two or three years ago... people...
This is my second album, this is the shirt

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:46.020
that came out with it. It comes with a poster,
seventeen songs on it, and we also just reprinted

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.430
these shirts; they were originally in green,
and now they're in black. My next album will

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:54.209
hopefully be coming out in, uh, the month
after this one. What is that? Um, April, May,

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:57.599
June. In June. That's all! Okay, bye!

